t(3, 2515, """The Chinese and the Russians do not see any pressing necessity to enter a military conflict with the United States! When China announced weeks ago that it is about to retake Taiwan in 2027, did it mean what I am going to write now?""")

t(4, 205, """I personally know nothing of the secrets of international politics, meaning what goes on in closed rooms, but it is enough for me to watch the American economy, then the global one, to decipher some of the riddles. Is China betting on the bursting of the American artificial intelligence bubble, calmly and unhurriedly watching for a decisive moment in which the bubble collapses in the United States, to enter Taiwan militarily?

The answer may be (yes) without exaggeration. So what does the collapse of the artificial intelligence bubble in the United States mean? The matter is truly frightening, because it will mean the collapse of a huge part of the American macroeconomy, not because artificial intelligence is the sector dominating the macroeconomy in the United States, but because it is the sector intertwined with everything related to modern technology, including even the basics of the internet industry! The shock may lead to a comprehensive collapse in an economy piled on top of itself and intertwined to the point of madness, as has never happened before in human history!

If China is waiting for that moment, it is right to a great degree and is not waiting for an illusion, but the matter is not in China's hands alone, because China must ask itself: if China knows, and the political world knows, and the world of individuals like us analyzes in order to understand and so knows, then does the United States not know?!""")

t(4, 890, """The size of the global real estate market in market value is 393 trillion dollars, and the size of the global artificial intelligence market is 372 billion US dollars, with a market value reaching 2.8 trillion dollars.

It is said, and I do not believe it, that in 2030 humans will lose 2 billion jobs .. meaning 2 billion people will become unemployed because of artificial intelligence .. while the correct figure may be no exaggeration if it is said that 8 billion people will be left without income! So is artificial intelligence a real war on the human race? And will this war on man end soon?

Many, when they deal with the economy, may separate the two sectors, and the problem, or one of the problems, since the problems are many, one of the problems is that the United States as a model, and behind it the whole world, at the level of investment all practise the culture of circular financing: real estate finances artificial intelligence, and artificial intelligence finances real estate. Most dangerous is that all sectors have come to practise circular financing, in which several companies from different sectors intertwine and finance one another to reach common goals; the fall of one sector means the fall of circular financing, and its fall means not the collapse of the collapsed sector alone but the collapse of the remaining sectors like dominoes. As we see, the world of economy in 2025 is playing dangerous games, and it has not been playing them only since 2025; the matter began long ago.

The bubble whose bursting economists talk about is sometimes described as a real estate bubble like the one that occurred in 2008, while others talk about the bursting of the artificial intelligence bubble .. The truth is that we must note that today's problem does not resemble 2008. In 2008 the greatest share of the collapse belonged to the real estate sector, with effects no one missed at the time, hitting the banking sectors, maritime shipping and logistics in general, and other sectors .. But the scale of the entanglement in 2025 is far greater and more complex than in 2008, and the global economy is heading toward losing its passion, because even the companies that spent hundreds of billions of dollars buying artificial intelligence technology have, to this moment, reaped nothing of real value. Some say openly today that artificial intelligence is a lie and a bubble, and that the companies manufacturing artificial intelligence technology, headed by Nvidia and Alphabet, are only selling the world an illusion; they make artificial intelligence components and data processors and exaggerate in describing their value as at the level of reaching the peak of the great industrial revolution, whereas the great industrial revolution in reality, and this is very clear, is still very far out of reach through the use of what is sold today to the world's companies for hundreds of billions, with those companies promised that by buying data storage devices and the like they will be an immediate part of the fourth industrial revolution, while the companies find nothing of this and do not move to any fourth industrial revolution. It is as if the matter were a clear deception and a selling of illusion, so that we can pose an important question: do Nvidia, Alphabet and others make components whose technical and operational value is exaggerated? The answer to this question is almost clear to many!

In conclusion, when the world discovers one morning that what it spent was a mere illusion, how many circular financing contracts will be torn up? And how many major, not minor, companies in the world will be torn apart that morning?!""")

t(4, 2315, """The manufacture of the craze ... and opening the tap, then suddenly closing it!! The craze, too, is always manufactured, in the science of social economy, throughout history, through the studied strategies of the policy makers!

In 2022 the greatest craze in human history was launched .. Advanced artificial intelligence, not the primitive kind. This craze is a craze because the greatest danger threatening those who rule the world is man's reaching the fourth industrial revolution. So why, then, did the major powers allow the world's craze for artificial intelligence, companies and individuals, to grow, as long as they believe that reaching the fourth industrial revolution, if it happens, will finish off humanity, when 8 billion people will sit on the street pavements, all of them unemployed, to begin burning the world, burning artificial intelligence and burning the artificial intelligence factories? For what I am saying is not hidden from the major powers that sponsor artificial intelligence today, and it is supposed to be self-evident!""")

t(5, 190, """Yet despite that, they, as the United States, China, the European Union and others, support artificial intelligence, its development and its growth. The reason is that artificial intelligence technology brings trillions of dollars to those who control the artificial intelligence technology industry, so the matter is collecting money for a while! Collecting as much money as possible, but on condition that if the world reaches the critical stage, all artificial intelligence technology must be eliminated, but after collecting the greatest amount of money!

Let us imagine the world when Microsoft appeared over it, at the beginning of man's craze for the computer, when people began buying computers! How much did Microsoft and the United States reap then?! Then how much did China reap when it joined in manufacturing computers? That global human craze for the bulky computer first, then the laptop, brought trillions to those who sold this craze to people!

The same thing is happening at a very high and accelerating pace, far bigger than the craze manufactured by Microsoft and IBM, and it is the artificial intelligence craze! Today the world is buying artificial intelligence tools and technology at the level of companies, not individuals, and those companies are buying with billions of dollars. But when artificial intelligence reaches the danger point! Danger to the major powers themselves! When it reaches this critical point, it will be brought down and got rid of, after the major powers have sold technology for trillions of dollars and reaped enormous sums from the whole world and from the pockets of all the world's companies by selling the illusion of moving to the fourth industrial revolution!

Companies buy and spend, and loans of hundreds of millions of dollars may be taken to build infrastructure in institutions so that those institutions become a global partner in the fourth industrial revolution; then suddenly the companies that make this technology fall, and with them falls the illusion of artificial intelligence, and with them evaporates the dream of the fourth industrial revolution, which is the greatest enemy of humanity in human history and the greatest security threat to 190 states in the world! As for the major powers, they will not release the devil into their streets to burn everything in them, because the fourth industrial revolution is the devil in flesh and blood; if that terrifying revolution is launched and 8 billion people become unemployed, the whole world will burn and no one will be spared! The answer: the major powers cannot bring themselves down, even if the theories of conspiracy against mankind are true, and they are true, but everything has a limit! The military complexes are what rule the world in America, China, Russia, the European Union, India, Pakistan and all the world's hotbeds of tension, and they are complexes far stronger than many of the opposing internal alliances that do not care about the stability of states because they have a different agenda, and these may in some way influence the ruling military complexes; but always, in every history and course of history, there are moments of truth and moments when the parties turn on one another, and there are never any rules or laws governing politics; this is a sentence with which I conclude, for those occupied with political analysis.

The picture can be understood well, but the results will always be human reactions, not strategic planning as they have always tried to suggest. When the bull falls into a pit, all the elegant strategies presented in a pedantic manner evaporate, the stage of emotions begins to run in the chemistry of the mind, global parties that were not on record begin, and floundering becomes the ruler over things and the title of what follows, because however much man tries to play clever, he will not be able to change the nature of his creation. As for pedantry in front of television screens and the show of strength east and west, these are political games, local consumption and propaganda, while man with his armies is far weaker.""")

t(5, 1635, """The end of the era of canned foods, sugars, hydrogenated oils and bran-stripped bread""")

t(6, 1100, """The third great war has nothing to do with Ukraine .. Ukraine is merely a peg to convince the European citizen that there is a case of defending morals and noble values and that the Russian danger to Europe is real, and these are two inaccurate reasons being marketed to the European citizen! The cause of the war, whether for Europe, the United States or the rest of the West, and the cause of the war for Russia and China, for all of them, has nothing to do with Ukraine or Taiwan .. These are all pegs .. The cause is that the world has reached a completely blocked road in the economy, and without a war (of breaking), as happened in the first and second world wars, the world will declare its bankruptcy, the global economy will collapse, and then no one will be able to fight anyone, because the money will not exist to finance a brawl in a narrow alley! Then the great powers see that this scenario is more dangerous than a third world war, and they are right in that! Because the collapse of the economy all at once without a world war will mean the disintegration of all states from within and the collapse of the security system in all its directions and forms, and this too will mean a world war, but not between the major powers, rather a world war of another kind! A war between every street and street in every city, and between every residential neighborhood and neighborhood in every city .. A global civil war that may last a thousand years without stopping if it breaks out! So yes, it is far more dangerous than a world war between major powers! A thousand times more dangerous than a war of the armies of world powers! The great powers grasp all of that, for it is a matter that can be grasped merely by analyzing it, pondering it and working to understand it, so the states will not be incapable of grasping it!""")

